WEBVTT

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.100
We've come home.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.380
<b>The Strongest Team</b>

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.470
I wonder what's for lunch today.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.460
Sazanka! Asagao!

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.340
Let's go eat!

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.550
Hurry, hurry!

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.340
Hurry! Hurry!

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.080
What's going on?

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.570
I heard Dokudami and the others are back!

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.690
Team Boar?

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.940
Right now they're divvying up boar meat!

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.090
<i>Lunch... Meat...</i>

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.070
<i>Lunch. Meat.</i>

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.480
<i>Lunch! Meat!</i>

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.750
<i>Lunch! Meat! Lunch! Meat!
Lunch! Meat! Lunch! Meat!</i>

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.900
Meat!

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.120
A-Asagao!

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.170
Why don't we go, too?

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.120
What about lunch?!

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.040
We'll do that after we 
say hello to Team Boar.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:44.510
Team Boar?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.440
See? Rindou has yet to meet them.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.500
Let's go.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.400
I don't mix well with them.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.850
Okay, come and get it!

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.540
We haven't had boar meat in a while!

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.760
I think I'll make some jerky.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.690
Sure, you do that!

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.800
Team Tiger is tiny, 
so I'll give you a biggish helping.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.200
Yay!

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.280
Much appreciated.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.600
Asagao is huge...

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.600
so you get even more!

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.110
Dokudami, you're the best!

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:36.190
Team Boar is a very good-natured trio.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.400
Oh, yeah?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.280
And if nothing else, they're strong.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.030
Dokudami wields a big club.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.530
Aogiri's sword is so fast, you can't see it!

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.290
Shakuyaku is nimble, and accurate 
at targeting weak points.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.000
In terms of offensive strength, 
they're probably the top team in Akane Class.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.380
She said they came back.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.060
Had they gone somewhere?

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.590
Yes. Those three have a particular weakness.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.890
They were on a journey to overcome it.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.180
Hey, Dokudami.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.390
Since you're back, 
does that mean you conquered it?

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.810
Yeah, we nailed it.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.980
We came up with a secret technique.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.690
No worries, now.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.350
Wow!

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:27.410
Now we truly are the strongest team!

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.080
Oh! That's right.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:36.920
There's a word that you must 
never say to Team Boar.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.160
A word you don't say?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.800
Yes.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.560
If you <i>do</i> go and say it...

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.760
This is incredible, though.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.880
How'd you bring down a big one like this?

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.640
I can take down one like 
this with a single swing!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.290
Oh, yeah?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.440
As always, you're stupid-strong!

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.400
Stupid-strong!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.220
Stupid-strong!

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.900
Stupid-strong!

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.650
Stupid-strong!

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.410
Stupid! Stupid!

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.620
And that word is—

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.830
Help me!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.160
You just had to say "stupid"!

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.870
Did you really say it?!

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.620
I didn't say "stupid"!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.390
You said it again.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.270
Quickly! This way!

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:43.500
All I said was stupid-<i>strong</i>, you know!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.540
Please hear us out, Dokudami!

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.070
Asagao didn't mean to—

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.840
Being made fun of is the 
one thing I can't stand.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.040
You know there's a price to pay!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.620
Let's just give them Asagao, Nee-sama!

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.300
I don't want you to desert me, you know!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.560
Move aside, Tsubaki.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.900
I challenge you to a duel in Asagao's place.

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:31.950
How about at two o'clock 
at the practice clearing?

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.290
Huh... With you, Tsubaki?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:38.080
Interesting. I accept.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.330
So, then...

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.170
Come and get your boar meat!

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:45.580
Here you go.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.300
Thank you very much.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.570
Sazanka, you better eat a bunch, too.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.550
I've never seen you before.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.810
This is Rindou. She transferred 
here from another village.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.980
Oh, yeah? Nice to meet you.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.900
N-Nice to meet you, too...

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.110
Then, I'll toss in a share for you, too.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.490
Th-Thanks.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:16.000
Team Boar likes to keep things 
separate in their minds.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.080
It makes them all the scarier.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.750
Okay, then.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:24.540
Might as well go say hi 
to Sensei before the duel.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:33.740
Wh-What're you doing?! 
Someone could get hurt!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.550
Sorry about that.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.200
Okay, see you later!

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.270
What the heck?!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.690
Stupid Asagao!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.880
Causing trouble for Nee-sama!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.230
Yeah, well...

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.530
But well played, Nee-sama.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.660
<b>Dog</b>

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.660
<b>A
k
a
n
e

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.290
We'll be fine, for now.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:55.660
You can't be too careful.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:57.950
I need to prepare.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:03.000
There's no point in that. 
They'll never show up, you watch.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.880
They won't? What do you mean?

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.590
Didn't Nee-sama say so?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.370
They have a weakness.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:12.770
Nobody in Team Boar has 
any sense of direction.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:14.510
Whatsoever.

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:17.770
S...

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.020
Sense of direction?

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:25.190
Yup! They've never reached 
where they're trying to go.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.600
And they'll never make 
it to where the duel is.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.230
I hope you're right.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.610
You'll be fine, Nee-sama!

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.130
So let's dry some meat instead!

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.570
They'll come.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.330
They said they have a sense of direction now.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.220
Hey!

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.760
Oh, Mokuren! It's been a long time!

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:57.930
That it has.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:01.830
I heard you're going to duel with Tsubaki.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.350
Yeah! Word travels fast.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.440
Don't hurt each other too badly!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.820
I can't guarantee that.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.820
The only thing I can do is go all out!

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:22.620
I'll go make lots of salve.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.390
Dokudami, it's time.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.080
Oh? Okay.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:29.920
Well, we're off to the clearing,

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:36.260
using the surefire secret technique 
we worked out on our journey!

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.570
L-Let's go home, Nee-sama! 
You're going to get hurt!

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.390
I was the one who suggested it.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.000
I'm not about to back down.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:56.560
But!

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.470
Besides...

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.410
I kind of look forward to 
getting to fight Dokudami.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.550
Oh, there you are!

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:16.830
Mokuren...

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:18.460
We thought you were them!

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:22.240
Sorry! I had something to tell Tsubaki!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.560
What is it?

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.540
Well you see, Team Boar probably won't show.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.440
Huh?

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.650
Or maybe more like, they can't.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:36.180
Looks like they still have 
no sense of direction!

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:40.290
B-But, they said something 
about some secret technique!

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:43.300
Oh, that's probably...

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:53.470
Right.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.590
This way!

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.410
Yeah, let's go!

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:59.950
They can't get away from us.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:01.350
Looks like they go whichever 
way the club falls.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.350
It's kind of hard to walk.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.690
Just you wait, Tsubaki!

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.690
Be careful. It might be a trap.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:14.190
Is Team Boar...

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:15.940
stupid or something?

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:16.460
They're stupid.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.030
And how.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.410
<b>Nee-sama</b>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.210
My face feels so bare.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.260
You can't sleep?

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:46.150
Do you feel anxious without
your mask after all?

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:53.060
I'm slowly getting used to it, I guess.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.940
Nee-sama.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:01.780
Hey, why does Sazanka call you "Nee-sama"?

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.100
You can't actually be sisters.

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:12.540
All right, I'll talk about 
the past until we get sleepy.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.920
"Today we decide teams."

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.760
<b>Today we decide teams.
Everyone gather at the mountaintop hut.
—Hana</b>

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:22.150
"Everyone gather at the mountaintop hut."

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.220
So it says.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.710
Decide teams?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.930
<b>Today we decide teams.
Everyone gather at the mountaintop hut.
—Hana</b>

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.020
What to do?

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.590
Want to go together?

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:28.200
Sure.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.770
What's wrong, Tsubaki?

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:34.470
I'm wondering why we need to 
gather all the way up there.

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:35.200
I'll be the first at the top!

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.610
Well, won't we find out if we go?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.060
Would you like to go together?

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:56.690
Sazanka is always by herself.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:59.390
You know how she is. Just leave her be.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.050
Tsubaki.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.640
Want to race to the top?

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:08.260
Fine by me.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.370
That decides it!

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:11.200
U-Um, Senpai...

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.840
Hey, you. Start us off.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.060
It's not "you," it's "Touwata"!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.720
I'll do it, but I have some conditions.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.660
Please let me be in the race, too.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.410
And if I win, you'll train—

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:25.130
Right, right. I'm cool with that.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.410
Make it snappy.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.300
All right, here goes.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.710
Ready, start!

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.980
I'm winning this thing today!

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.380
Help!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.440
Somebody!

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:51.680
Hey, Tsubaki!

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:52.930
We're in a race!

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.040
Please go on ahead!

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.030
I'll catch up!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.300
I can't move.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.530
What happened?

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.070
Sazanka happened!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:06.440
Again!

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:13.080
Back then, Sazanka played pranks on 
everyone, and was always causing trouble.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:14.630
Huh.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.370
That might not be so different from now.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.980
Perhaps you're right.

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:23.840
And so?

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.280
And so, where's Sazanka?

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.300
She went that way.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.620
I hope I don't end up on her team.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.850
Why do you feel that way?

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.760
Because she's always doing such nasty things.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:46.070
Like the other day.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:58.970
"It's your fault for 
getting caught," she said!

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.750
She's mean!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.880
Fuki, don't cry.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.800
It's okay. There's nothing 
to be scared of now.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.490
We're here for you.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:09.190
Mhm.

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:10.770
It's okay, it's okay.

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:11.670
There, there.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.550
I'll go look for her!

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:15.490
Huh? What for?!

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:16.510
Forget about her!

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:18.670
Hey! What about our race?!

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:23.310
Sazanka! Where are you?!

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.700
Please answer!

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.190
Great...

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.200
It's all slippery around here.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.470
As soon as I said it!

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:45.710
Sazanka!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.960
Good, this is where you—

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.390
Are you here to scold me?

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:51.760
Like always.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.720
Well, yes and no.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:00.740
Let's go.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.670
Sazanka?

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:07.750
No.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.730
Why not?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.740
Won't we be assigned a team 
when we get to the top?

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:17.660
I don't want to be on anyone's team.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:45.690
I'm pretty sure you'll be on 
a team, even if you stay here.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:21.930
We're going!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.680
No! I don't wanna!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:24.710
Let go!

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:25.590
Ow!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.870
Did you twist your ankle?

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:37.530
Put me down!

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:39.700
Stop it! Put me down!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.560
Please don't struggle!

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:44.280
Then put me down! Don't you hear me?!

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:46.330
You can't make it to the summit alone!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.790
I don't want to go!

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.290
I can't stand you, Tsubaki!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.090
I can't stand... any of you!

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.440
Th-That was close!

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.390
Sorry about that.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.100
Let's get going.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:23.230
Why do you dislike us? Me and the rest.

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:28.250
Well, none of you like me anyway.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:32.380
Is that why you do things on 
purpose to make us dislike you?

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.710
You could just be brave 
and get along with us.

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.640
I don't know how...

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.480
Well, I like you, Sazanka.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:52.650
That's the first step toward getting along.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.090
Hey, whatcha doing?

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.530
Asagao.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:09.710
What happened to your feet?

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.370
You match, huh?

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.710
Beni-senpai, wait up!

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:22.900
Please start training!

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.660
If I feel like it.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:29.100
We made it!

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:31.350
You're so helpful, Asagao!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.960
And strong.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:34.810
Aren't I?

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.960
I see you hurt your legs.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.650
Go see Konoha later for treatment.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.530
S-Sensei!

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:41.570
What is it, Sazanka?

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:47.190
Well...

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:53.210
I-I want to be on Tsubaki's team!

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:56.420
B-Because I like her.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.940
Sensei! I'd like that, too!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:05.010
We already have a way of deciding teams.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:09.970
Whomever you reach this summit 
together with, they're your team.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.500
That's long been the custom.

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:14.420
Then...!

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:20.030
Therefore, Tsubaki, Sazanka, Asagao,

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:23.390
the three of you are now Team Dog.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.430
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:30.290
And that's how we came to be Team Dog.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.260
And then, after that...

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:40.020
Maybe the story ran a little long.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:58.020
Hey, Sazanka. Did you know?

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.110
My name is Tsubaki.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:02.950
Yeah, I knew that.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:07.240
"Tsubaki" and "Sazanka" are 
in the same flower family.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:12.200
Does that make them sisters?

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:14.380
I suppose it does!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.120
I look forward to spending time with you!

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:27.160
Me, too, Nee-sama.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:06.100
We've decided down to Team Dog, 
and that just leaves three girls.

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:16.240
Where the heck are those last three, 
and what are they doing?

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:19.500
It's practically a straight 
path up the mountain.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.770
Well, they're the last, 
so that makes them Team Boar.

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:27.050
If three of us happened to meet here...

00:23:27.320 --> 00:23:30.470
...it must mean we're going the right way!

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.010
I'd say so.

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:34.320
Good for us!

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:35.170
Let's go.

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:35.970
Yeah.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:40.520
<b>Next time:

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:39.250
To be continued!
